    "explanation": "Both parties have, in the end, done the same arithmetic, and the record supports it. This is a rider-filed dispute over the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee charged on TRP-09102, and the question is whether the driver earned it under POL-NS-01.\n\nAll four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold on this trip's own admissible evidence. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 22:40:20. (b) The GPS trace places the driver 24.0 m from the pickup pin (derived driver_track.max_distance_m 24.01 m over 51 qualifying fixes) at and before that timestamp, well inside the 150 m arrival radius the fee schedule sets for the AIRPORT zone class, and the qualifying run starts at 22:40:00, before the 'arrived' tap. (c) The continuous in-geofence dwell runs from the first qualifying fix at 22:40:00 to cancellation at 22:48:20, which is 500 seconds against the 480-second AIRPORT minimum - a surplus of 20 seconds, and the clock is run from the first in-geofence fix, not from the 'arrived' event, exactly as limb (c) requires. (d) The trip shows no boarding event and was terminated by the driver at 22:48:20, twenty seconds after the required dwell elapsed, on cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises.\n\nNo clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the charge, and I answer each route the advocates raised. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not engage: it governs only a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m, whereas here the driver was 24.0 m from the pin, inside the radius. POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered) fails at limb (b): the rider wrote 'I am walking over now' at 22:41:40 and the driver replied 'Okay, I will remain at Door 5' at 22:41:58, eighteen seconds later, inside the 120-second window, so the clause does not apply whatever the reply said. Limb (c) also fails affirmatively on the rider's own track - 519.47 m from the pin on its 24 fixes, with 0 qualifying fixes inside the 200 m AIRPORT rider-presence radius - but limb (b) alone closes this route. POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) does not engage: matched to the 22:40:20 event the driver sat 24.0 m from the pin at 0.0 km/h, far inside the 300 m distance threshold and below the 15 km/h motion threshold, so no waiting clock is recomputed. POL-NS-06 (waiting-period shortfall) does not engage: the 500-second run against the 480-second minimum leaves a shortfall of -20.0 seconds, that is, no shortfall at all, and the trace shows a single in-geofence interval with no excursions, so the limb (i) accumulation question is never reached.\n\nOn the money: POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee itemised in the fare breakdown, which is SGD 4.80 (80 percent of SGD 6.00), the residual SGD 1.20 being the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not bite - driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the four-termination limb, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d 120 is 0.008, below the 0.08 rate limb, and the clause requires both - so compensation is not withheld. The SGD 6.00 charge itself reconciles with the fee schedule: the AIRPORT zone-class fee is SGD 6.00 and the RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee is SGD 6.00, and the resolution rule takes the greater, so there is no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d).\n\nOn weight and escalation: the deciding facts are carried by the GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown and driver profile, all at admissibility weight 1.0 with no issue codes, so nothing that decides this case is discounted. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09102-01 (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed, but no surviving claim builds on it and the trace shows a single in-geofence interval, so it carries no deciding fact and does not cap confidence or trigger escalation. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: neither profile shows disputes_with_counterparty_90d (both 0), rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, the anti-farming check has not tripped, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The driver's counterparty statement corroborates his account of waiting at Door 5 and replying promptly, consistent with the trace and chat log. Because the ruling moves money to the driver, amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both carry the same figure, SGD 4.80; the rider's charge stands as itemised. No clause in this category produces a referral on these facts."
